<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-6296] Show note name in the New UI&apos;s page title when entering a note, like Classic UI</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-6296</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;Classic UI&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13078086/13078086_%E1%84%89%E1%85%B3%E1%84%8F%E1%85%B3%E1%84%85%E1%85%B5%E1%86%AB%E1%84%89%E1%85%A3%E1%86%BA+2025-08-25+%E1%84%8B%E1%85%A9%E1%84%92%E1%85%AE+9.18.14.png&quot; height=&quot;204&quot; width=&quot;579&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In Classic UI, the tab title is displayed as &#8220;Zeppelin&#8221; on the main page. However, when entering a note, the title changes to the note&#8217;s name (left tab: main, right tab: note view).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;New UI&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13078085/13078085_%E1%84%89%E1%85%B3%E1%84%8F%E1%85%B3%E1%84%85%E1%85%B5%E1%86%AB%E1%84%89%E1%85%A3%E1%86%BA+2025-08-25+%E1%84%8B%E1%85%A9%E1%84%92%E1%85%AE+9.19.04.png&quot; height=&quot;204&quot; width=&quot;578&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In contrast, in the New UI the page title is fixed as &#8220;Zeppelin&#8221; on all pages. It seems necessary to modify this to behave like the Classic UI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
